#  Tooltips. One entry per tooltip, broken into lines with \n: a translation is not the
#  same length as the English and has to wrap in its own places. Eight lines of about
#  fifty characters is what the tooltip box holds.
vivecraftx.tooltip.reverseHands=Swap left/right hands as dominant\n  ON: Left dominant, weirdo.\n  OFF: Right dominant
vivecraftx.tooltip.worldScale=Scales the player in the world.\nAbove one makes you larger\nAnd below one makes you small\nAnd the ones that mother gives you\ndon't do anything at all.
vivecraftx.tooltip.worldRotation=Adds extra rotation to your HMD.\nMore useful bound to a button or \nchanged with the arrow keys.
vivecraftx.tooltip.worldRotationIncrement=How many degrees to rotate when\nrotating the world.
vivecraftx.tooltip.playModeSeated=Standing or seated play mode\nStanding is vastly superior.
vivecraftx.tooltip.resetOrigin=Recenter the player's feet in the world to 1.62m below the current\nHMD position. For non-lighthouse tracking systems.
vivecraftx.tooltip.menu.hud=Open this configuration screen to adjust the Head\nUp Display (HUD) overlay properties.\n  Ex: HUD size, HUD distance, Crosshair options
vivecraftx.tooltip.menu.stereo=Open this configuration screen to adjust the Head \n  Mounted Display optics or other rendering features.\n  Ex: FOV, Distortion, FSAA, Chromatic Abberation
vivecraftx.tooltip.menu.locomotion=Configure the locomotion based settings: movement\nattributes, VR comfort mode etc...
vivecraftx.tooltip.menu.interaction=Configure what your hands reach, hit and open,\nand how much of your own body you can see.
vivecraftx.tooltip.menu.profiles=Open this configuration screen to manage\nconfiguration profiles.
vivecraftx.tooltip.movementMultiplier=Sets a movement multiplier, allowing slower movement\nthan default. This may help reduce locomotion induced\nsimulator sickness.\nWARNING: May trigger anti-cheat warnings if on a\nMultiplayer server!!\nDefaults to standard Minecraft movement (1.0)\nspeed).
vivecraftx.tooltip.walkUpBlocks=Allows you to set the ability to walk up blocks without\nhaving to jump. HOTKEY - RCtrl-B\nWARNING: May trigger anti-cheat warnings if on a\nMultiplayer server!!\n  OFF: (Default) You will have to jump up blocks.\n  ON:  You can walk up single blocks. May reduce\n       locomotion induced simulator sickness for some.
vivecraftx.tooltip.inertiaFactor=Sets the player's movement inertia in single player\nmode. Lower inertia means faster acceleration, higher\ninertia slower accelaration. High inertia may reduce\nmotion sickness for some, but beware of cliff edges!!\n  Normal: (Default) Standard Minecraft player\n           movement.\n  Automan < Normal < A lot < Even More. Does not\n  affect lava, water or jumping movement currently.
vivecraftx.tooltip.simulateFalling=If enabled the player will falls to the ground in TP mode\nwhen standing above empty space. Also allows jumping
vivecraftx.tooltip.allowModeSwitch=Allows the use of the Pick Block button to switch between\nTeleport and Free Move mode.
vivecraftx.tooltip.moveMode=Current move mode. Teleport or Free Move.
vivecraftx.tooltip.limitTeleport=If enabled the arc teleporter will be have restrictions\nin survival mode. It will not be able to jump up the side\nof blocks, it will consume food, and it will have an energy\nbar that refills over time.
vivecraftx.tooltip.bcbOn=Shows your body position as a square shadow on the ground.\nThis is your Square Shadow Buddy (tm).\nDo not lose your Square Shadow Buddy.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticJump=If turned on, once you jump in real life\nYour player will also jump. Also enables\nJump Boots.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticSneak=If turned on, once you duck in real life\nYour player will also sneak
vivecraftx.tooltip.smoothTurnSpeed=How fast the world turns when turning is smooth,\nin degrees a second. Only used when the turn step\nis set to SMOOTH.
vivecraftx.tooltip.joystickDeadzone=How far a stick must move before it counts.\n  Raise this if you drift or turn slowly while\n  holding nothing.
vivecraftx.tooltip.fovReductionMin=How far vision narrows while you are being moved.\n  Lower closes in further. This is the strongest\n  comfort setting there is: it covers the edges of\n  vision, which are what make people ill.
vivecraftx.tooltip.teleportHorizLimit=How far a teleport may carry you along the ground.\n  This is the figure that decides how much of the\n  walking teleporting replaces.
vivecraftx.tooltip.teleportUpLimit=How far a teleport may carry you upwards.\n  One block is a step up. More than that starts\n  replacing climbing.
vivecraftx.tooltip.teleportDownLimit=How far a teleport may drop you.\n  A few blocks is a jump you could have made\n  anyway; a lot is a way out of anywhere.
vivecraftx.tooltip.calibrateHeight=Stand up straight and press this.\n  Tells the mod how tall you are, which is what\n  the fixed view height holds you at and what\n  decides how far you can reach.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticDismount=Get out of a boat or cart by stepping out of it,\n  instead of pressing a key.
vivecraftx.tooltip.worldHaptics=Feel what the world does to you, not only what\n  you do to it: being hurt, burning, low health,\n  rain on your hands.
vivecraftx.tooltip.chatHaptics=A slight nudge in the off hand when somebody\n  says something in chat.
vivecraftx.tooltip.fixedHeight=Stops the view following the headset up and down.\n  For playing lying down or slumped back. Your head\n  is held at your standing height and your hands come\n  with it, so they stay where you expect them.\n  Crouching, swimming and riding still move the view.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticClimb=If turned on, allow climbing ladders and vines\nby touching them. Also enables Climb Claws.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticSwim=If turned on, allow swimming by doing the breaststoke\nwith the controllers.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticRow=Row, row, row your boat... by flapping your arms like mad.
vivecraftx.tooltip.walkMultiplier=Multiplies your position in the room by a factor\nAllows you to walk around more,\nbut may cause motion sickness
vivecraftx.tooltip.freemoveMode=The source for freemove direction. Options are\nController: Uses left controller direction, max speed\nHMD: Uses head direction, max speed\nRun In Place: Use average controllers direction. Speed based\non controller motion.\nJoy/Pad: Uses the left touchpad or joystick for all motion.\nOverrides all 4 movement direction keybinds.
vivecraftx.tooltip.vehicleRotation=Riding in a vehicle will rotate the world\nas the vehicle rotates. May be disorienting.
vivecraftx.tooltip.fovReduction=Shrinks the field of view while moving. Can help with\nmotion sickness.
vivecraftx.tooltip.weaponCollision=If enabled, you can swing your pickaxe at blocks to\nmine them, or your sword at enemies to hit them.
vivecraftx.tooltip.onlySwordCollision=Whether anything in your hand can hit things, or\nonly a sword. Everything else then passes through\nthe world without touching it.
vivecraftx.tooltip.swordBlockCollision=Whether swinging a sword at a block mines it.\n  Off is calmer: a sword then only cuts what a\n  sword is for, and walls survive a stray arm.
vivecraftx.tooltip.reducedPlayerReach=Whether another player has to be reached with the\nweapon itself rather than with the swing around it.\n  Keeps a wide gesture from stabbing a bystander.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticBlockInteract=Put a hand on a lever, a chest or a door and press\nthe interact button, instead of pointing at it.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticEntityInteract=Put a hand on a creature and press the interact\nbutton to pet, milk, shear or saddle it.
vivecraftx.tooltip.animalTouching=If enabled, touching a passive mob (animal) without a\nweapon will right-click (interact) instead of attacking.\nTurn off for Piggy Slapping, Josh.
vivecraftx.tooltip.realisticOpening=Hitting a door, gate, hatch, lever or button\n  works it instead of mining it.
vivecraftx.tooltip.renderOwnBody=Draws your own body below you, so you can see\n  yourself when you look down.
vivecraftx.tooltip.splitArms=Bends the arms at the elbow to reach where your\n  hands actually are, instead of holding them straight.
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudOpacity=How transparent to draw the in-game HUD and UI
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudHide=Whether to hide the in-game HUD or not.\n  YES: The HUD is hidden.\n  NO:  The HUD is visible.
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudScale=Relative size HUD takes up in field-of-view\n  The units are just relative, not in degrees\n  or a fraction of FOV or anything
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudPitch=The vertical offset of the HUD, in degrees.\n  Negative values are down, positive up.
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudYaw=The horizontal offset of the HUD, in degrees.\n  Negative values are to the left, positive to\n  the right.
vivecraftx.tooltip.physicalKeyboard=Which keyboard appears when you ask for one.\n  IN WORLD: one standing in front of you that you\n       poke with your fingertips. Stays where you\n       put it and works without window focus.\n  STEAMVR: SteamVR's own, which floats over\n       everything and is off in seated mode.
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudWristOffset=How far along your forearm the wrist HUD sits.\n  Higher values move it back towards the elbow,\n  lower ones towards the hand. Only used when\n  the HUD is locked to the wrist.
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudDistance=Distance the floating HUD is drawn in front of your body\n  The relative size of the HUD is unchanged by this\n  Distance is in meters (though isn't obstructed by blocks)
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudOcclusion=Specifies whether the HUD is occluded by closer objects.\n  ON:  The HUD will be hidden by closer objects. May\n       be hidden completely in confined environments!\n  OFF: The HUD is always visible. Stereo depth issues\n       may be noticable.
vivecraftx.tooltip.renderMenuBackground=Specifies whether the in game GUI menus have a \nsemi-transparent background or not.\n  ON:  Semi-transparent background on in-game menus.\n  OFF: No background on in-game menus.
vivecraftx.tooltip.hudLockTo=Specifies to which orientation the HUD is locked to.\n  HAND:  The HUD will appear just above your off-hand\n  HEAD:  The HUD will always appear in your field of view\nstraight ahead\n  WRIST:  The HUD will appear on the inside of your off-hand\narm. It will 'pop out' when looked at.
vivecraftx.tooltip.touchHotbar=If enabled allow you to touch the hotbar with\nyour main hand to select an item.
vivecraftx.tooltip.renderCrosshairMode=Set the in-game crosshair display mode\n  Always:   The crosshair is always shown even if the\n            HUD is disabled\n  With HUD: The crosshair is only shown when the HUD\n            is enabled\n  Never:    The crosshair is never shown
vivecraftx.tooltip.crosshairScale=Sets the size of the in-game crosshair
vivecraftx.tooltip.menuCrosshairScale=Sets the size of the menu crosshair
vivecraftx.tooltip.renderBlockOutlineMode=Sets the in-game block outline display mode.\n  Always:   The block outline is always shown even if\n            the HUD is disabled\n  With HUD: The block outline is only shown when the\n            HUD is enabled\n  Never:    The block outline is never shown
vivecraftx.tooltip.crosshairScalesWithDistance=Determines how the crosshair changes with distance.\n  ON:   The crosshair will grow larger in the distance to\n   remain the same apparent size from your viewpoint.\n  OFF: The crosshair will always be the same size\n   in the world and appear to shrink with distance.
vivecraftx.tooltip.crosshairOcclusion=Whether the crosshair is hidden by anything\n  closer than what it is pointing at.
vivecraftx.tooltip.chatFadeAway=What becomes of a chat line once it has arrived.\n  Fades: it fades out after a few seconds, the way\n   it does on a monitor.\n  Stays: the latest lines stay on the panel until\n   newer ones push them off, for when you were\n   looking at the world and not at your wrist.
vivecraftx.tooltip.fsaa=Uses a fancier method of resampling the\ngame before sending it to the HMD. Works best\nat high render scales. 
vivecraftx.tooltip.renderScalefactor=The internal rendering scale of the game, relative\nto the native HMD display. Higher values improve visual\nquality, espeically with FSAA on, at the cost of performance
vivecraftx.tooltip.mirrorDisplay=What the monitor shows while you are in the headset.\nCropped fills the window, Single eye fits the whole\neye into it, Both eyes shows the pair side by side.
vivecraftx.tooltip.mirrorCrop=How much of each edge the cropped mirror throws away.\nThe outer edge of an eye is distorted by the lens and\nis not really visible in the headset anyway.
vivecraftx.tooltip.mirrorEye=Which eye the single-view mirror modes show.
vivecraftx.tooltip.mirrorGui=Draws the interface flat on top of the mirror, so it\nis readable on the monitor. It is in the world either\nway; this is for whoever is watching.
vivecraftx.tooltip.monoFov=The FOV used for the undistorted mirror mode.
vivecraftx.tooltip.stencilOn=Mask out areas of the screen outside the FOV.\nImproves performance.
vivecraftx.tooltip.vrHotswitch=Shows the game on the monitor when you take the\n  headset off, and goes back to VR when you put\n  it on again.
vivecraftx.tooltip.vrRemember=Starts in whichever mode you left the game in,\n  rather than in VR every time.
vivecraftx.tooltip.vrToggleButton=Puts a VR on/off button on the main menu.
vivecraftx.tooltip.vrCloseWithRuntime=What to do if SteamVR shuts down while the game\n  is running: quit, or carry on without VR.
vivecraftx.tooltip.button.defaults=Resets all values on this screen to their defaults
vivecraftx.tooltip.keyhole=The number of degrees to the left and right of center\nWhere the view will begin to rotate.
vivecraftx.tooltip.xSensitivity=Speed the view will rotate when pushed on the edge of the keyhole
vivecraftx.tooltip.ySensitivity=Vertical speed of the crosshair related to the mouse
vivecraftx.tooltip.seatedMoveMode=Free Move with WASD or Teleport with W
vivecraftx.tooltip.seatedHudXhair=The direction the HUD will be placed.\nHMD view direction or crosshair pointing direction
vivecraftx.tooltip.seatedHmd=Which way is forward when you walk: where the\n  headset is looking, or where the crosshair points.
